22
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:05,000
First up the drums.

23
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:09,000
As per usual I always sort of categorize the sounds I'm making.

24
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:19,000
Bass drum, snare drum, hi-hat, some breaks I used, some extra ultrasounds and some intro synth percussions.

25
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:21,000
Let's jump right in.

26
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:23,000
As you can hear.

27
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:32,000
Seneth's verse is complemented by this synth percussion loop here that is sort of playing the melody as the bass line does.

28
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:40,000
And sort of to give the vocal like a fundamental backend if you like.

29
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:42,000
There comes a little break here.

30
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:47,000
Pretty standard stuff, filtered stuff.

31
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:54,000
Some hi-hats there, kick build to increase the tension or whatever.

32
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:56,000
And then it drops.

33
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:03,000
What's maybe a bit special here is that the kick groove is a bit off.

34
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:10,000
You can tell it's a bit shifted to the right relative to the time.

35
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:13,000
And there's six kicks in one bar which is quite a lot.

36
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:15,000
I think usually it's like four or three.

37
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:20,000
And what's also maybe special is that none of the kicks actually have a lot of bass with them.

38
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:26,000
Not a lot of sub, all of them end in sort of 60Hz, 70Hz of range.

39
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:34,000
And only one kick here has some more low end to it just because of how the groove came together.

40
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:36,000
As you can see here.

41
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:44,000
It's like an off kick that sort of plays against the groove.

42
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:47,000
So that had a bit more space to get more low end.

43
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:50,000
Snare pretty standard.

44
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:55,000
Sign fundamental with a couple of layers.

45
00:03:55,000 --> 00:04:00,000
As you can hear those are the main characteristic ones.

46
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:05,000
Which are bounces from the actual snare which was created here.

47
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:08,000
Which is still in there for the intro.

48
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:13,000
Which had a different low end, a different fundamental which was higher.

49
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:19,000
And as I went with the project I felt like pulling the fundamental frequency lower down.

50
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:21,000
Closer to where the bass is.

51
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:26,000
It even makes the space more narrow and more claustrophobic.

52
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:28,000
Which I really liked with this song.

53
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:31,000
Really intense in the low mids.

54
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:34,000
That's how the snare came together.

55
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:37,000
Second 16 again is just a render of those guys.

56
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:40,000
Just really shortened with an audio file here.

57
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:45,000
But same top line here, top end here.

58
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:47,000
And then it goes back into the original groove.

59
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:49,000
Original snare, sorry.

60
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:51,000
Hi-hats really reduced actually.

61
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:54,000
If you look at this in the first bar there's only one.

62
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:58,000
