63
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:02,000
Even though the song is really busy there's not a lot of hi-hats there.

64
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:05,000
And they just evolve as the song goes.

65
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:07,000
More stuff coming in.

66
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:12,000
Until they in the second 16 release in this shaker loop here.

67
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:18,000
That sort of transforms into just a noise at the end of the bar.

68
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:20,000
And it just disappears really.

69
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:26,000
And then we're coming back third 16 with a shaker vibe.

70
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:29,000
A little amen break here.

71
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:31,000
And that's that really.

72
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:34,000
So the drums are really simple I'd say.

73
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:38,000
It's all about just trying to figure out which hits you need.

74
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:41,000
I could have also dropped with a lot of hi-hats.

75
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:45,000
But it's all about the contrast of this full section here.

76
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:48,000
It's really dense over the top almost.

77
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:53,000
And then it sort of falls into this void almost.

78
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:59,000
Which was the most essential part for me about this song.

79
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:03,000
Why I sort of finished it and why I like it.

80
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:07,000
So what I'm trying to say is that the drop doesn't always have to be full on.

81
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:10,000
Top band, hi-hat, overhead, this and that.

82
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:12,000
Sometimes simplicity is the way to go.

83
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:15,000
